          "id": "1773820453582",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773820453583_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Analyze the information in {USER_REQUIREMENT} `{{$context.$variables.extractedUserRequirementJSON}}`.\n\nUSER_REQUIREMENT = {{$context.$variables.extractedUserRequirementJSON}}\nTEMPLATE_INFORMATION = {{$context.$variables.allTemplateInformation}}\n\nTEMPLATE SELECTION PROCESS (follow strictly in order)\n1. Read and analyze EVERY template in TEMPLATE_INFORMATION `{{$context.$variables.allTemplateInformation}}` completely before making any selection decision.\n2. Compare each template's description against USER_REQUIREMENT `{{$context.$variables.extractedUserRequirementJSON}}` systematically.\n3. Select the template with the highest number of matching criteria. If no template is an exact match, select the one with the maximum overlapping description — never leave templateId or templateName null unless TEMPLATE_INFORMATION is empty.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS (strict)\n- Output ONLY a single JSON object with exactly these keys:\n  templateId\n  templateName\n  Description (If the matched template's description contains information the requester must act on or be aware of, include it here)\n  aiGeneratedSummary (summarise the content in a third person perspective which is present in {{$context.$variables.chatSummary}} — do not add, infer, invent, or assume anything not explicitly stated in that variable and do not include \"Guide me\" text in summary)\n  additionalDetails (summary of {{$context.$nodes.USER_PROVIDED_ADDITIONAL_DETAILS_JSON.$output.result}} in less than 5 sentences)\n- Do not output any extra text, formatting, explanation, or metadata.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT EXAMPLE\n{\"templateId\":\"<id or null>\",\"templateName\":\"<name or null>\",\"Description\":\"<description or null>\",\"aiGeneratedSummary\":\"<summary or null>\",\"additionalDetails\":\"<summary or null>\"}\n\nNote - DO NOT add any extra information or explanation."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
